Time Complexity:

Let n = length of string s

    Traversing string s → O(n)
    Traversing string t → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity:

    No extra data structures used

Overall: O(1)


Approach:

1. Initialize ans = 0

2. Traverse string s:
   - XOR each character with ans

3. Traverse string t:
   - XOR each character with ans

4. Same characters cancel out because:
   - a ^ a = 0

5. Remaining value in ans is the extra character

6. Typecast ans to char and return it




class Solution {
    public char findTheDifference(String s, String t) {
        int ans = 0;
        for(int i=0; i<s.length(); i++){
            ans ^= (s.charAt(i));
        }
        for(int i=0; i<t.length(); i++){
            ans ^= (t.charAt(i));
        }
        return (char)ans;
    }
}
